---
code: cfg-builtin-shadowed
when-fires: a book funcdef shadows a shell builtin the engine relies on (dash resolves a function before a regular builtin). cfg.rs warn_shadowed_relied_builtins.
why: find-I: builtin-dependent conclusions may be unsound for this book. The hole is typed: `{name}` is the shadowing function, which is also the builtin it shadows; the sentence is the code's own register. The primary span is the funcdef name_span.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
test() { hork --stub; }
if test -f /etc/nginx/nginx.conf; then
  apt-get install -y nginx
fi

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh > /dev/null
cfg: warning[cfg-builtin-shadowed]: Function `test` shadows a shell builtin Dorc
relies on: analysis keeps reading the bare word `test` as the builtin, so
conclusions that lean on it may be unsound for this book.
      [ book.sh:2:1
   2 | test() { hork --stub; }
     | \__/
probe: note[site-unresolvable]: sm 1 site run unprobed (no read-only check could
be shipped): `apt-get install -y nginx` -- run `dorc why` for the per-site
detail (the apply runs each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:4:3
   4 |   apt-get install -y nginx
     |   \______________________/

   = help:  sm site runs `apt-get install -y nginx`
hint: 'apt-get' (line 4) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
dorc: plan-summary sites=2 elide=0 omit=0 guard=0 run=2 may-alias=0
dorc: decision-digest 8f4c77928c33f49ca45ba67f92159157a728e1ddb0b2bd0b79719e27e3c9e719

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: cfg-builtin-shadowed
{{name}} = "test"
{{count}} = "1"
{{site_word}} = "site"
{{v0}} = "book.sh"
{{v1}} = "0"
{{v2}} = "0"
{{v3}} = "0"
{{v4}} = "2"
{{v5}} = "0"
